WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.815
OT business continuity protects critical physical operations, not just servers.

00:00:04.815 --> 00:00:07.960
It defines how the organization maintains an acceptable service,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.005
shifts to a safe degraded mode, performs a controlled shutdown,

00:00:11.005 --> 00:00:13.740
and restores trustworthy operation after disruption.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.640
Planning begins with essential processes and their dependencies: controllers, HMIs,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.340
engineering systems, networks, utilities, people, vendors, spares, facilities,

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.750
and downstream operations.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.060
Recovery objectives must reflect process state, safety, data tolerance,

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.855
and the real time needed for validation and restart.

00:00:29.855 --> 00:00:34.335
Backups should cover logic, configurations, system images, data, software, licenses,

00:00:34.335 --> 00:00:35.940
and vendor-specific requirements.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.900
Protected copies and restore testing prove recoverability.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.035
Manual fallback is useful only when equipment, procedures, staffing,

00:00:42.035 --> 00:00:44.095
and training make it safe and sustainable.

00:00:44.095 --> 00:00:48.700
During cyber incidents, continuity and incident response coordinate containment, fallback,

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.580
safe shutdown, evidence preservation, and deliberate recovery.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.675
Speed alone cannot justify reconnecting systems whose integrity or dependencies remain

00:00:55.675 --> 00:00:56.415
uncertain.

00:00:56.415 --> 00:01:00.340
Strong programs exercise decisions, drill procedures, test restoration,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.740
maintain contacts and diagrams, assign owners, and close lessons learned.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.375
Continuity is a practiced organizational capability aligned with safety and operational

00:01:08.375 --> 00:01:09.060
reality.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:09.955
Its purpose is safer,

00:01:09.955 --> 00:01:13.620
more predictable recovery of the mission when normal systems and assumptions fail.
